  "question": {
    "text": "Consider two identical rings of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;fixed on a horizontal axis in a gravity-free space. A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m&nbsp;</mi></math>is held at rest at the centre of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math>&nbsp; ring and projected along the axis towards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp; ring. The minimum speed of projection so that the particle reaches the centre of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp; ring is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0023836_Question_1..jpg\" style=\"width: 309px; height: 217px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
